# Copy to himalaya-accounts.local (gitignored) and fill with real accounts.
# This committed example uses placeholders only — never real addresses.
#
#   cp scripts/himalaya-accounts.example scripts/himalaya-accounts.local
#
# Globals:
#   @key|value
# Accounts (one per line, 12 fields):
#   name|email|display_name|imap_user|imap_url|smtp_user|smtp_url|starttls|pass_title|folders|default|mailapp
#
# folders: generic | icloud | gmail
# starttls / default / mailapp: true|false
#
# Passwords are NOT in this file. Himalaya uses password.command → pass-cli
# (title + --field password). Mail.app profiles inject passwords at generate
# time only; the .mobileconfig is local, 0600, never git.

@display_name|Your Name
@downloads_dir|~/Downloads
@pass_vault|Personal
@mailapp_payload_id|com.example.mail.imap.mail-only
@mailapp_payload_name|IMAP mail@

# Extra IMAP (hosting) — flag mailapp=true for the addresses you want in Mail.app.
example-mail|mail@example.com|Your Name|mail@example.com|imaps://imap.example.com:993|mail@example.com|smtp://smtp.example.com:587|true|mail@example.com (Example IMAP)|generic|false|true
example-spam|spam@example.com|Your Name|spam@example.com|imaps://imap.example.com:993|spam@example.com|smtp://smtp.example.com:587|true|spam@example.com (Example IMAP)|generic|false|false

# iCloud IMAP (one account; custom-domain From addresses are identities on this mailbox)
icloud|you@icloud.com|Your Name|you|imaps://imap.mail.me.com:993|you@icloud.com|smtp://smtp.mail.me.com:587|true|Himalaya (Apple)|icloud|true|false

# Gmail IMAP (app password item — not the Google account login)
gmail|you@gmail.com|Your Name|you@gmail.com|imaps://imap.gmail.com:993|you@gmail.com|smtps://smtp.gmail.com:465|false|Himalaya (Google Mail)|gmail|false|false
